cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SeraEdit in research, please cite the accompanying SoftwareX article and this software release."
title: "SeraEdit: Reliable Language-Guided MusicXML Editing through Structured Score Patches"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Gao"
    given-names: "Yuan"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-0394-3623"
    affiliation: "Zhejiang Conservatory of Music"
version: "1.0.0-dev.14"
date-released: 2026-08-23
repository-code: "https://github.com/Selancee/Sera"
url: "https://github.com/Selancee/Sera"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - MusicXML
  - symbolic music
  - score editing
  - large language models
  - research software
abstract: >-
  SeraEdit is a local-first research software system for converting natural-language
  score-editing instructions into versioned, source-bound ScorePatch transactions.
  It validates schema, score structure, protected scope, musical constraints, and
  MusicXML round trips before a revision can be reviewed or applied.
